InsacredTexts: {
	Cooldown: Recharging: {0} s
	Fic0: The Devourer of Gods tore through the fabric of reality one last time and found Signus waiting for him on the other side. "I told you I would come back," he whispered... then they kissed.
	Fic1: Draedon had not left his laboratory in three hundred years. Yharim walked in, set down a cup of coffee next to the Exo Mech blueprints and stayed... then they kissed.
	Fic2: The Old Duke surfaced from the Sulphurous Sea, reeking of acid rain. Amidias silently handed him a towel... then they kissed.
	Fic3: Cryogen and the Brimstone Elemental met halfway between the Snow biome and the Brimstone Crag, steam rising from the ground between them... then they kissed.
	Fic4: The Tax Collector counted every single coin Draedon owed him. Draedon counted every single second until he would leave... then they kissed.
	Fic5: Crabulon slowly turned its mushroom-covered head toward the Hive Mind. Neither of them had a mouth, but that had never stopped anyone... then they kissed.
	Fic6: The Dragonfolly landed on the edge of Yharon's nest, feathers ruffled by the storm. For once, Yharon did not breathe fire... then they kissed.
	Fic7: Permafrost brewed two cups of hot chocolate, frost still clinging to his beard. Cirrus finally sat down across the table... then they kissed.
	Fic8: The Ebonian Paladin and the Crimulan Paladin had been arguing for an hour about which color was the best. The Slime God sighed, and the two slimes blushed... then they kissed.
	Fic9: The Polterghast had wandered the Dungeon alone for centuries. One night, the Dungeon Guardian turned around... then they kissed.
	Fic10: The Desert Scourge finally reached the Ocean, where the Aquatic Scourge had been waiting for ten thousand years... then they kissed.
	Fic11: Astrum Deus split itself in two to fight harder, then looked at its other half for a very long time... then they kissed.
}
